    {
      "id": "template-library-task-overview",
      "type": "markdown",
      "label": "Good Artifact Contracts",
      "position": {
        "x": -220,
        "y": -420
      },
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "width": 560,
      "height": 240,
      "data": {
        "markdown": "## Good Artifact Contracts\n\nA **good artifact** satisfies the previously established Twilite graph standards appropriate to its role and is composed from required pieces that satisfy the contracts beneath it. Goodness is compositional: higher layers may delegate, but they may not conceal broken required promises. Optional pieces may degrade only through an explicit fallback.\n\n### Good Node\n\nA good node:\n\n- follows the established identity, ownership, data, visibility, port, handle, binding, and authority standards;\n- exposes or can resolve the authored semantic views appropriate to browsing: glyph, icon, summary/card, and detail, plus an editor when the node is editable;\n- uses a declared fallback chain when a richer view is unavailable;\n- keeps domain provenance separate from runtime-reserved view-resolution fields;\n- produces precise diagnostics for any view, binding, handle, or authority it declares but cannot resolve.\n\nA node instance may resolve these surfaces through its class. It does not need to duplicate class-owned view definitions.\n\n### Good Node Class\n\nA good node class:\n\n- is itself a standards-compliant class graph with a canonical root;\n- defines the data contract, editor, glyph/icon/summary/detail surfaces, fallbacks, and stable semantic meaning for its instances;\n- exposes a real bridge granting the bounded authority required to create and resolve instances;\n- is built from valid lower-level views, ports, and class machinery.\n\n### Good Template\n\nA good template:\n\n- is itself a good, standards-compliant graph composed from good required nodes and classes;\n- exposes a canonical root, useful preview, and concise authoring or installation guidance;\n- declares whether it derives a whole graph or installs a bounded capability;\n- exposes an export bridge describing the exported nodes, edges, bridges, authority, collision rules, and singleton constraints;\n- distinguishes graph-owned identity, IDs, save paths, and navigation from library-owned class, edge, view, and authority references;\n- enrolls automatically in the Templates collection and survives a Save-As-style derivation smoke test.\n\n### Composition Law\n\nA good class is built from good lower-level pieces. A good template is built from good classes and nodes. A derived graph becomes a good graph by preserving those contracts while acquiring its own identity and address.\n\n**Valid** means an artifact makes no broken declared promises. **Good** means it fulfills the complete useful contract expected of its advertised role.",
        "_classBinding": {
          "key": "markdown",
          "sourceRef": "github://twilite-zone/public/library/classes/nodes/markdown.node-class.node",
          "ref": "github://twilite-zone/public/library/classes/nodes/markdown.node-class.node",
          "identity": {
            "graphId": "markdown_class",
            "name": "markdown Node Class",
            "version": "0.1.0",
